menu "XPRS over XPRS-WiFi (long range)"

config XPRS_WIFI8
    bool "XPRS-WiFi bearer (the xwifi library)"
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32C3 || IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
    default n
    help
        Carries XPRS packets over XPRS-WiFi, the long-range chirp-spread-
        spectrum waveform of the xwifi library, on the chip's own 2.4 GHz
        radio -- about 24 dB more link budget than the ESP-NOW bearer, bought
        with seconds of airtime per packet instead of a single frame.

        The radio is shared with the ordinary 802.11 stack (the walk-up
        hotspot and the local-WiFi uplink) by time-slicing: 802.11 most of the
        time, borrowed for short XPRS-WiFi slots. The AP and the uplink hiccup
        for each slot, so the slot length and cadence (xprswifi8_cfg_t) are a
        tuning knob, not a fixed number.

        Offered only on the ESP32-C3 and ESP32-S3, the chips xwifi has a port
        for. On a C3 running the full station the 128 KiB I/Q bank the port
        reserves may not fit beside everything else -- measure the free heap
        on a C3 build before relying on it. Everything compiles to nothing
        when disabled.

endmenu
